          <para id="para-00024">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para id="para-00025">All three lines intersect at \((1, 2)\). If students graph \(8y=16\), the graph of
            the new equation is a horizontal line. If students graph \(8x−2y=4\), the graph of the
            new equation is a new line between the two original lines.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
