    <section id="sect-00004">
      <note class="self-check" id="note-00002">
        <para id="para-00089">Solve the system of equations using elimination. Check the
        solution by graphing.</para>
        <para id="para-00090">
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}&amp;&amp;\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x\;–\;4y\;=\;–26\\-3x\;+\;4y\;=\;29\end{array}\right.\end{array}\)</para>
      </note>
    </section>

    <section id="sect-00005">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00006">
        <title>Adding Systems of Equations and Using Their Graphs</title>
        <para id="para-00091">Look at the system of equations shown here:</para>
        <para id="para-00092">
          \(\begin{array}{rcl}&amp;&amp;\left\{\begin{array}{l}–3x\;+\;4y\;=\;7\\3x\;+\;2y\;=\;17\end{array}\right.\end{array}\)</para>
        <para id="para-00093">Let’s graph each equation on the coordinate plane. Identify the point of intersection.</para>
        
          <media alt="GRAPH OF TWO LINES INTERSECTING AT THE POINT (3, 4).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_06_08_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
     
        <para id="para-00094">The lines intersect at \((3, 4)\).</para>
        <para id="para-00095">Add the two equations together. Simplify the resulting equation.</para>
        <para id="para-00096">\(\begin{array}{r}-3x+4y=7\\3x+2y=17\\\hline6y=24\\y=4\end{array}\)</para>
        <para id="para-00097">Graph the resulting equation on the same coordinate plane.</para>
        
          <media alt="GRAPH OF THREE LINES INTERSECTING AT THE POINT (3,4).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_06_08_02.jpg"/>
          </media>
        

        <para id="para-00098">All three lines intersect at \((3, 4)\).</para>
        <para id="para-00099">You verified that by adding the two equations in the system, you created a third
          equation that is also true.</para>
        <para id="para-00100">The solution to the system is \(x = 3\), \(y = 4\).</para>
        <note class="try look-at-me" id="note-00003">
        <title>Try It: Adding Systems of Equations and Using Their Graphs</title>
        <para id="para-00101">Add the equations to find the resulting equation. Then graph all three equations to
          find the ordered pair where they intersect.</para>
        <para id="para-00102">Use this system of equations to answer questions 1 – 4.</para>
        <para id="para-00103">\(\left\{\begin{array}{c}-2x-3y=7\\2x+y=3\end{array}\right.\)</para>
        <!--Q#1-->
        <exercise id="exer-00018">
          <problem id="prob-00023">
            <para id="para-00104">Add the equations to find the resulting equation.</para>

          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00023">
            <para id="para-00105">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00106">
              \(\underline{\;\;\;\;\;-2x-3y=7\\+\;\;\;\;\;\;\;2x+y=3}\\\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;-2y\;=10\\\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;y\;=-5\\\)</para>
            <para id="para-00107">
              \(9\begin{array}{rcl}2x+\;y&amp;=&amp;3\;\\2x+\;(-5)&amp;=&amp;3\\2x&amp;=&amp;8\\x&amp;=&amp;4\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <!--Interaction
        End -->

        <!--Q#2-->
        <exercise id="exer-00019">
          <problem id="prob-00024">
            <!--QUESTION
            IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
